# Docker build context.
#
# The documented build is `docker build -t traider .` — the context is the REPO
# ROOT, because the Dockerfile copies `src/`. Docker only honours a
# `.dockerignore` sitting at the context root, so THIS is the file that applies;
# the one in `docker/` would only count for a build whose context is `docker/`,
# which cannot work (no `src/` there). Keep the two in sync if that changes.
#
# Without this file the context included `.venv` (≈520 MB) on every build.

# --- secrets: never in the context, never in the image -------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- docs / repo metadata: not needed inside the image -------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
docs
README.md
*.md

# --- local environments --------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
ENV
env

# --- runtime data & generated output (large, regenerated locally) --------
data/
logs/
tmp/
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log

# The live strategy store is your own data; the container creates its own.
strategies/store.json

# --- Python caches -------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytype/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- OS / editor noise ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
